# Ductus trust/governance boundaries.
#
# These entries record who owns the paths that protect the way of working and
# make GitHub request the owner's review automatically. They are NOT a merge
# gate: the "Require review from Code Owners" branch protection setting is
# deliberately OFF (docs/ENGINEERING_SYSTEM.md section 10), because the owner is
# the only code owner and GitHub does not let an author approve their own PR.
# It may be switched on only after a second real code-owner identity exists
# (issue #53). Until then the machine protection is the risk floor, independent
# App-authenticated review/QA and, for D-97 paths, the owner's merge command.
#
# The last matching rule wins; keep every rule owned so no later, broader rule
# can clear an earlier owner. tests/unit/codeowners.test.ts checks that every
# D-97 path (D97_PATHS in scripts/orchestrator/orchestrator-core.mjs) is covered.
